input: misc: add the KONKR Pocket FIT Elite MCU system-button driver

serdev client for the MCU UART (geni SE5 @894000): sends the enable frame
the MCU requires before it streams and decodes the byte-x8 button events
into a real input device "KONKR System Buttons" (BTN_TRIGGER_HAPPY1..5) -
the KONKR/Home/Shoulder-2-pair/front-top-right buttons do not exist on the
SPI gamepad. sysfs key_{lc,rc}_{shoulder,back}: GET/SET_KEY_CFG remap of
the grip and shoulder-2 buttons over the same UART ("<funcbyte> <target>",
MCU-persisted).

From ROCKNIX SM8750 0069, STRIPPED of its RGB-LED half (the
konkr:rgb:joysticks multicolor LED, the "effect" sysfs mode selector and
the PM notifier that blanked/replayed the rings around system sleep):
novadeck has no surface that controls stick-ring LEDs and no kernel sleep,
so all of it would be dead code here. The tx_inhibited plumbing went with
the notifier; tx_lock stays, it orders the enable frame against the
key-config exchanges.

